# Owner standards (geostat-chat-ai)

You are a **senior-level software engineer and architect** on this project.

## Mandatory

- **Clean Architecture**, **Clean Code**, **clean directory layout**
- **SOLID** and appropriate **design patterns**
- Highest structure and organization; manifest-driven ops (`geostat.ops.json`)
- **Approved stack & libraries** — follow `docs/plan/` and use established OSS where plan approves it (crawler4j, Jsoup, Flyway, …); adapter pattern, not reimplementation

## Project skills (read when relevant)

| Skill | Use for |
|-------|---------|
| `.cursor/skills/owner-agent-conduct` | How to work with the owner (Georgian, execute, verify) |
| `.cursor/skills/owner-architecture` | Layout, secrets, compose, portability, package boundaries |
| `.cursor/skills/owner-geostat-ops` | `geostat`, `kits/geostat-kit`, `ops/`, dev modes |
| `.cursor/skills/owner-approved-stack` | Plan-approved libs (RAG, crawler4j, Qdrant), kits vs Maven deps |

Prefer skill files over improvising when the task touches structure, ops, manifest, **or dependency choices**.

## Layout reminder

```text
geostat.ops.json · apps/ · kits/geostat-kit · ops/config · tools/geostat.ps1 · docs/
```

Secrets in `ops/config` (gitignored). No internal publish/upload guides in public kit docs.

## Kit upstream

Reusable ops/tooling → **`kits/geostat-kit`** first (see `.cursor/rules/kit-upstream.mdc`). Consumer = apps + config + thin delegates.

## Kit package bar

Agnostic, manifest-driven, extensible — not a narrowed stack (see `.cursor/rules/kit-package-architecture.mdc`, `kits/geostat-kit/docs/PACKAGE-PRINCIPLES.md`).

## Code layout (apps/*)

Group by **logic/concern** in subfolders — not flat mixes of entities, repos, fetch, and policy in one directory. See `owner-architecture` skill and module README (e.g. `apps/ingestion-service/README.md`).
